               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nWe have learned two friendly new tables:\n\n- Multiplying by 8 means adding the number eight times, which is the same as counting by eights: 8, 16, 24, 32, 40...\n- Multiplying by 9 means adding the number nine times, which is the same as counting by nines: 9, 18, 27, 36, 45...\n\nWe used an octagon with eight sides for the table of eight, and an enneagon with nine sides for the table of nine. We also saw that 8 × 9 = 72 and 9 × 8 = 72. Changing the order of the factors does not change the product. (<htcite0>)\n\nKeep practicing with real objects — count the sides of octagons by eights, count the sides of enneagons by nines — and explore the interactive tables again. You will see that these two tables always work.",
